    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "A strategic shift to lifecycle management... okay, that's an interesting way to look at it. But if I'm going to pitch this to the rest of the partners, I can't just say \"growth is flat.\" I need to explain why this actually validates their long-term vision. If the growth engine is \"working in a different way\" like you said, how would you frame the recent data to show that their actual trajectory is still incredibly strong, even if the raw numbers look steady right now?",
